# PostgreSQL SCRAM-SHA-256: the 4 authentication packets

Captured: `psql` to PostgreSQL 16, SCRAM-SHA-256-PLUS over TLS (Wireshark).

## Field legend

| Field | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `p=tls-server-end-point,,` | GS2 header (channel binding requested). Only in packet 1 |
| `n=` | username (empty; PostgreSQL uses the startup packet user) |
| `r=` | nonce (client nonce, then client nonce + server nonce) |
| `s=` | salt, base64 |
| `i=` | PBKDF2 iteration count |
| `c=` | channel binding, base64 = `p=tls-server-end-point,,` (24 B) + SHA-256 of server certificate (32 B). `biws` (= `n,,`) when no channel binding |
| `p=` | ClientProof, base64, 32 B |
| `v=` | ServerSignature, base64, 32 B |

## Packet sequence

| # | Frame | Direction | Message |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 26 | client -> server | `p=tls-server-end-point,,n=,r=W9IrGgf7LpsssNerOGIcRDsi` |
| 2 | 27 | server -> client | `r=W9IrGgf7LpsssNerOGIcRDsiydppEs2LhXHu8Sr8JdXg9NOy,s=fClpg1M4eimzY/nhx7yXwA==,i=4096` |
| 3 | 28 | client -> server | `c=cD10bHMtc2VydmVyLWVuZC1wb2ludCwsoOrQ7hsneQb55KEH9ESx9N9shQ9GArcNRhgZbGJjvBk=,r=W9IrGgf7LpsssNerOGIcRDsiydppEs2LhXHu8Sr8JdXg9NOy,p=YTVtTIH+nOxhSAvKouKvpnOVTfop5Pl7KYw4CLnnlHg=` |
| 4 | 29 (first `R`) | server -> client | `v=EZPTqUbeJP2JjL6ZBedZuNdAWzuji6vfKYip00YBNPA=` |

Frame 25: server offers mechanisms. Frame 29 (`<R/R/S x14/K/Z`) also carries AuthenticationOk, 14 ParameterStatus, BackendKeyData, ReadyForQuery.

