## Packet 1: client-first

```
p=tls-server-end-point,,n=,r=<client nonce>
```

---

## Formulas (before packet 2)

Stored on the server at password-set time (`pg_authid.rolpassword`):

```
SCRAM-SHA-256$<i>:<salt>$<StoredKey>:<ServerKey>
```

```
SaltedPassword  = PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256(password, salt, i)
ClientKey       = HMAC-SHA256(SaltedPassword, "Client Key")
StoredKey       = SHA256(ClientKey)
ServerKey       = HMAC-SHA256(SaltedPassword, "Server Key")

AuthMessage     = client-first-bare + "," + server-first + "," + client-final-without-proof
ClientSignature = HMAC-SHA256(StoredKey, AuthMessage)
ClientProof     = ClientKey XOR ClientSignature
ServerSignature = HMAC-SHA256(ServerKey, AuthMessage)
```

AuthMessage parts for this capture:

| Part | Value |
|---|---|
| client-first-bare (packet 1 minus `p=tls-server-end-point,,`) | `n=,r=W9IrGgf7LpsssNerOGIcRDsi` |
| server-first (packet 2) | `r=W9Ir...NOy,s=fClpg1M4eimzY/nhx7yXwA==,i=4096` |
| client-final-without-proof (packet 3 minus `,p=...`) | `c=cD10...jvBk=,r=W9Ir...NOy` |

Joined with `,`. No spaces. `c=` and `s=` stay base64 text.

