## Packet 2: server-first

```
r=<client nonce + server nonce>,s=<salt>,i=<iterations>
```

Server nonce appended: `ydppEs2LhXHu8Sr8JdXg9NOy`. Salt and `i` come from the stored verifier.

### State after packet 2

| Value | Client | Server |
|---|---|---|
| Password | yes | no |
| Client nonce | yes | yes |
| Server nonce | yes | yes |
| Salt | yes | yes |
| Iterations `i` | yes | yes |
| SaltedPassword | computes | no |
| ClientKey | computes | no |
| StoredKey | computes | yes (stored) |
| ServerKey | computes | yes (stored) |
| client-first-bare | yes | yes |
| server-first | yes | yes |
| client-final-without-proof | builds | not yet |
| AuthMessage | computes | not yet |
| ClientSignature | computes | not yet |
| ClientProof | computes | not yet |

---

## Packet 3: client-final

```
c=<channel binding>,r=<combined nonce>,p=<ClientProof>
```

`c=` hash is computed by the client from the server certificate it received in the TLS handshake.

### State after packet 3

| Value | Client | Server |
|---|---|---|
| Password | yes | no |
| SaltedPassword | yes | no |
| ClientKey | yes | no |
| StoredKey | yes | yes |
| ServerKey | yes | yes |
| AuthMessage | yes | builds now |
| ClientSignature | yes | computes now |
| ClientProof | sent | received |
| Recovered ClientKey' | no | computes now |

### Server verification

```
AuthMessage     = client-first-bare , server-first , client-final-without-proof
ClientSignature = HMAC(StoredKey, AuthMessage)
ClientKey'      = ClientProof XOR ClientSignature
check           : SHA256(ClientKey') == StoredKey
check           : c= hash == SHA256(own certificate)
check           : r= == combined nonce sent in packet 2
```

| Result | Outcome |
|---|---|
| all equal | continue to packet 4 |
| mismatch | `FATAL: password authentication failed for user "..."` |

---

## Packet 4: server-final

```
v=<ServerSignature>
ServerSignature = HMAC(ServerKey, AuthMessage)
```

Followed in the same frame by `R` AuthenticationOk, 14x `S`, `K` (PID + cancel key), `Z` (ReadyForQuery, status `I`).

### Client verification

```
expected = HMAC(ServerKey, AuthMessage)
check    : expected == v=
```

| Result | Outcome |
|---|---|
| equal | login completes |
| mismatch | connection aborted, no query sent |

---

## Errors psql prints

Server rejects the proof (wrong password), produced by the server:

```
psql: error: connection to server at "127.0.0.1", port 5432 failed: FATAL:  password authentication failed for user "postgres"
```

Client rejects `v=` (server could not prove it holds the verifier), observed with a test server that sent a random `v=`:

```
psql: error: connection to server at "127.0.0.1", port 5433 failed: incorrect server signature
```

| Failure point | Checked by | Error source |
|---|---|---|
| ClientProof (`p=`) | server | `FATAL: password authentication failed` |
| ServerSignature (`v=`) | client (libpq) | `incorrect server signature` |

